{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1151075-i-have-no-idea-how-to-use-solar-performance-and-bureaucracy","id":1151075,"title":"I have no idea how to use Solar Performance and Bureaucracy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-19T11:38:53-07:00","id":1151075,"title":"I have no idea how to use Solar Performance and Bureaucracy","content":"<div align=\"center\"><img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/WOEPzSO.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/tgwMtae.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>Since I can't really find anything substantial on the Internet about the subject so figure that I should ask here. Basically I have some trouble at creating plothooks where characters with Performance and Bureaucracy charms feels really Solar-ly.<br /> <br /> For Performance, I feel a bit like a one-trick pony since the only plot that I can think of is those stereotypical scene in ancient drama shows where some hot girl dances/sings, some guy falls in love with her but he has a wife/girlfriends and they start fighting. But this is Exalted and I'm Jen, the hot girl is a burly Hellenic man and he steals the heart of the woman and her husband. There, that's the only thing that I can think of for Solar Performance....<br /> <br /> I'm more interested in the kind of plot that has various cultural things sprinkles in, so I tried to read about how various cultures treat music and dance, but reading about how music is a gift from gods or how it enhances the fabric of society still doesn't spark my imagination at all. I guess that the problem is that I'm still uncertain about how various characters/places in Creation think about music? Like, if Dai Sifu does decide to sing in a public place in city X, does everybody around him starts to whisper about such a good singer much surely being a messenger of misfortune since the local deity of death has the form of a bird-body woman?<br /> <br /> With Bureaucracy, I don't really care for the merchant aspect so what left is the bureaucrat side, which is a problem since this circle of Exalted constantly travels around. The only plothooks in my head right now for such an Eclipse is him being a kind of troubleshooter, basically when the Circle arrives at a new place, the Eclipse starts to observe and proceed to fix various social/legal/bureaucratic problems. Though that's a little bare bone (and seems more like a modus operandi than a plothook ...), so I would love it if people can help by giving some examples of your characters solving Bureaucracy problems.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":18}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T12:33:04-07:00","id":1151086,"title":"","content":"I admit, part of the trouble I've seen with the Bureaucracy charmsets that aren't related to Merchanting (and good buttery god I've gotten use out of THOSE with my Eclipse not-a-pirate) is that they seem to be built on the assumption that there's some kind of system for Bureaucratic projects.<br /> <br /> And there's, um, kind of not. Beyond 'Eh, wing it?'. Makes me wonder if there was some kind of system that took into account scope and speed of a project, but it got cut.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I haven't used anybody with Performance Supernal in-play. I have a concept for an ABYSSAL with Performance charms, but even then she's also a Necromancer and Exorcist, who uses her singing to lure in wandering ghosts for her purposes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T14:24:47-07:00","id":1151114,"title":"","content":"I don't think building plots around Performance or Bureaucracy (or any Ability, really) is how it's supposed to work. <br /> <br /> You can use Performance to cause distraction, gain access to entertainment venues, teach valuable life lessons, make pocket change, motivate armies, incite mobs, garner support for whatever your political cause is, etc. It's a tool you use to solve problems. You can very easily play a character who's just in it for the art (in which case the ST should build a plot around that, because it's the player's major goal for their character), but it's very easy to make it a means to an end rather than an end in and of itself. <br /> <br /> Bureaucracy is a little different. If you're heavily investing into it, it's assumed you're either a merchant or running your own organization or both. However, characters who travel a lot will benefit greatly from Speed the Wheels and Measuring Glance to run roughshod over any organization they encounter. You can walk into a city and immediately meet with with most important people around -- administrators, generals, merchants, criminals, gods, whoever -- and you can use Measuring Glance to see who is and isn't loyal to the organizations they belong to, which means you know who would be willing to betray their organization to you for a bribe or favour. <br /> <br /> A lot of it comes down to the ST and the players and the kind of game they want. If it's understood that the campaign will involve a lot of traveling, a character with Supernal Bureaucracy is not a good fit. That's true no matter what RPG you're playing though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T15:36:50-07:00","id":1151135,"title":"","content":"Possibly slightly overthought (and pretentious) ideas on Performance spurred off a little by trying to think about what you can do with them and about &quot;heroes of performance&quot;:<br /> <br /> 1) Performance is cool, because you get to roleplay being all the inspirational figures who wrote performed great poetry (Homer), or music (Mozart), or acting (er... Edward Alleyne?), and so on. And coming with that is the ability to influence culture and groups of people, and to reveal people's true feelings. (Think of every play-within-the-play that does this in media).<br /> <br /> 2) At the same time, I do think all the above can go to a slightly cynical place at times - you perhaps default to Mirror Flag, the poet-playwright who is really the secret 4D chessmaster, working to change the world politically. That's cool, but at the same time, focused on too much sells short art as a genuine act of communication and inspiration, and a genuinely human act, if we are defaulting to these characters who are *just* creating forms of manipulative propaganda or satire that doesn't touch anything deep and true and genuinely moving. In short terms, characters who *use* art, rather than characters who *express themselves* through art, or *create* art.<br /> <br /> Of course, this is not to say that, art isn't often made by astute creatives, who understand the politics of their time, and are aware enough to use them in their art to increase their standing, or avoid censure. But that is just one aspect.<br /> <br /> 3) The whole aspect of Solars as revolutionary upenders of world order, and their hunted status in the world order, seems like it can exacerbate the degree we go straight to 2) and limit our perspectives on Solars as artists. It *makes* *sense* for us to immediately start thinking of them as performers who are stuck in a situation where they have to use art slightly cynically.<br /> <br /> So I don't know if I can sum up, but think about characters who are have genuinely interesting convictions and beliefs and passions about the world, and want to express them, and are capable of doing so movingly and powerfully, and let the consequences play out in without having to tame all this within the bounds of &quot;intrigue&quot; and &quot;politics&quot;, strictly. I guess specifically for you Jen, if you're reading this (possibly not, because it is a big ramble), you are an artist, so maybe you can draw on your own experiences as an artist?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T17:31:39-07:00","id":1151163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1151075-i-have-no-idea-how-to-use-solar-performance-and-bureaucracy?p=1151135#post1151135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Possibly slightly overthought (and pretentious) ideas on Performance spurred off a little by trying to think about what you can do with them and about &quot;heroes of performance&quot;:<br /> <br /> 1) Performance is cool, because you get to roleplay being all the inspirational figures who wrote performed great poetry (Homer), or music (Mozart), or acting (er... Edward Alleyne?), and so on. And coming with that is the ability to influence culture and groups of people, and to reveal people's true feelings. (Think of every play-within-the-play that does this in media).<br /> <br /> 2) At the same time, I do think all the above can go to a slightly cynical place at times - you perhaps default to Mirror Flag, the poet-playwright who is really the secret 4D chessmaster, working to change the world politically. That's cool, but at the same time, focused on too much sells short art as a genuine act of communication and inspiration, and a genuinely human act, if we are defaulting to these characters who are *just* creating forms of manipulative propaganda or satire that doesn't touch anything deep and true and genuinely moving. In short terms, characters who *use* art, rather than characters who *express themselves* through art, or *create* art.<br /> <br /> Of course, this is not to say that, art isn't often made by astute creatives, who understand the politics of their time, and are aware enough to use them in their art to increase their standing, or avoid censure. But that is just one aspect.<br /> <br /> 3) The whole aspect of Solars as revolutionary upenders of world order, and their hunted status in the world order, seems like it can exacerbate the degree we go straight to 2) and limit our perspectives on Solars as artists. It *makes* *sense* for us to immediately start thinking of them as performers who are stuck in a situation where they have to use art slightly cynically.<br /> <br /> So I don't know if I can sum up, but think about characters who are have genuinely interesting convictions and beliefs and passions about the world, and want to express them, and are capable of doing so movingly and powerfully, and let the consequences play out in without having to tame all this within the bounds of &quot;intrigue&quot; and &quot;politics&quot;, strictly. I guess specifically for you Jen, if you're reading this (possibly not, because it is a big ramble), you are an artist, so maybe you can draw on your own experiences as an artist?</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue is that Performance has to be cynical to let us know the Solar Exalted are able to effect the appeals and attractiveness of virtue but don't have an express priority over it (that is tellingly the Sids whose schtick is all the universe is data programming with silly names). Great example Solars have few charms dealing with lighting up, commmanding nature OR revelation. Heck imitating the full effects of sunlight were taken away the moment a pcsplat had to worry about them. The Solars thing is Heroes as Great but Not Good. You ALWAYS have to face they are mighty but not good. so the PLAYERS make them good.<br /> <br /> Also Art as sublime communication kinda got picked up by the Demons and Rakhasa in the interim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1498-darmani","name":"Darmani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1498_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T17:43:11-07:00","id":1151165,"title":"","content":"Well, first thing that comes to mind when one speaks of solar Performance is figures like <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orpheus\" target=\"_blank\">Orpheus</a> or <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bres\" target=\"_blank\">Cairbre</a> of the Tuatha De Danann, whose poem about Bres' rule was so scathing and virulent it got him full of sores and warts - causing him to be declared imperfect and dethroned, for some examples.<br /> <br /> Also, performance is the skill tied to prayer if memory tricks me not, making it a sort of subtly interesting hotline with the spirit world as a whole - where does singing of the clouds beauty ends and praying/flirting a cloud spirit starts, so to speak...<br /> <br /> Does that help any?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T18:47:52-07:00","id":1151172,"title":"","content":"If you're looking for stories based on Performance, I could imagine a version of Arachne's hubris: you declare yourself the best dancer in the world and some other Exalt/the god of dance/the Brass Dancer himself takes umbrage and comes to express their displeasure, with optional dance battle.<br /> Bureaucracy suffers rather from the Sail problem, i.e. &quot;don't take Sail if you're not going to be sailing&quot;. But I've seen a charater with fantastic Bureaucracy fun turning a cult into an effective organization. Maybe there's something there: building your own organization, inspiring branches to pop up all over the place. You could invent the ATM aspect of banking or the postal system or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T19:48:52-07:00","id":1151191,"title":"","content":"Performance also covers Oration, so any of the parables or sermons of Jesus, or similar prophet figures can be inspiration. Echoing what was said earlier about actually playing Homer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T19:55:26-07:00","id":1151193,"title":"","content":"David also arguably has high Performance, and let's not forget Rinaldo from <i>The Phoenix on the Sword</i>. Lots of fun to be had, performing with such skill to move even a king.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T21:06:04-07:00","id":1151203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1151075-i-have-no-idea-how-to-use-solar-performance-and-bureaucracy?p=1151193#post1151193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">David also arguably has high Performance, and let's not forget Rinaldo from <i>The Phoenix on the Sword</i>. Lots of fun to be had, performing with such skill to move even a king.</div> </div> </div> </div>A king he <b>opposes</b>, no less!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T22:42:56-07:00","id":1151216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1151075-i-have-no-idea-how-to-use-solar-performance-and-bureaucracy?p=1151086#post1151086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit, part of the trouble I've seen with the Bureaucracy charmsets that aren't related to Merchanting (and good buttery god I've gotten use out of THOSE with my Eclipse not-a-pirate) is that they seem to be built on the assumption that there's some kind of system for Bureaucratic projects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Naah, the Bureaucracy system in Master of Jade seems pretty robust but I still can't think of anything interesting for the Eclipse to do.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1151075-i-have-no-idea-how-to-use-solar-performance-and-bureaucracy?p=1151135#post1151135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) At the same time, I do think all the above can go to a slightly cynical place at times - you perhaps default to Mirror Flag, the poet-playwright who is really the secret 4D chessmaster, working to change the world politically. That's cool, but at the same time, focused on too much sells short art as a genuine act of communication and inspiration, and a genuinely human act, if we are defaulting to these characters who are *just* creating forms of manipulative propaganda or satire that doesn't touch anything deep and true and genuinely moving. In short terms, characters who *use* art, rather than characters who *express themselves* through art, or *create* art.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh, this is the opposite of the Zenith in the comic, since performing is the only time where he isn't being faked. Now I want to have him and Mirror Flag meets just to see what happen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1151075-i-have-no-idea-how-to-use-solar-performance-and-bureaucracy?p=1151165#post1151165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, performance is the skill tied to prayer if memory tricks me not, making it a sort of subtly interesting hotline with the spirit world as a whole - where does singing of the clouds beauty ends and praying/flirting a cloud spirit starts, so to speak...</div> </div> </div> </div>It feels like most gods (and elemental?) has a positive Intimacy toward music and dance, there is an Artifact fans and erhu that can be used to attract spirits near you. I can definitely imagine a bunch of good scenes coming out of this idea. There is a sleeping Elemental Dragon near An-teng who will go on a rampage when he wakes up, I plan to just smack him around at first when I read about him, but I wonder if some heartfelt song would work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1151075-i-have-no-idea-how-to-use-solar-performance-and-bureaucracy?p=1151193#post1151193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">David also arguably has high Performance, and let's not forget Rinaldo from <i>The Phoenix on the Sword</i>. Lots of fun to be had, performing with <b>such skill to move even a king.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Both Orpheus and the girl in the Ex3 Performance's write-up uses this same trope i.e A musician uses their skill to make a person of authority feel emotional. It feels awesome since it happens only one time, but does it become stale if a Solar does this repeatedly?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 10-20-2017, 01:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T09:18:28-07:00","id":1151351,"title":"","content":"There's also the Pied Piper/Siren move, lulling a viscious brute or savage beast to sleep, inspiring an army, striking fear into the opposing camp, instigating or defusing riots, and of course defeating a tsunami with the power of rock.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13057-anathemouse","name":"Anathemouse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13057_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T12:14:56-07:00","id":1151418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1151075-i-have-no-idea-how-to-use-solar-performance-and-bureaucracy?p=1151216#post1151216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Naah, the Bureaucracy system in Master of Jade seems pretty robust but I still can't think of anything interesting for the Eclipse to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I wasn't using Master of Jade. I was referring to the Ex3 core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T12:43:37-07:00","id":1151424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1151075-i-have-no-idea-how-to-use-solar-performance-and-bureaucracy?p=1151216#post1151216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It feels awesome since it happens only one time, but does it become stale if a Solar does this repeatedly?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWell, how do you do that for anything else?<br /> <br /> \u200bI suggest that one thing that helps it be varied are the distinctions between the personalities and circumstances and the kinds of things that appeal to or provoke folks.<br /> <br /> \u200bSomebody brought up propaganda, and while that's a technically accurate term for a lot of what Performance could do, I think the term has issues with it being loaded by certain negative connotations (which, ironically, is an association that would itself result from a lot of propaganda). There's a matter of using your artistic expressions to shape the narrative of social or political events from a place of sincerity. I mean, love poetry about a specific person can constitute a form of propaganda, but that doesn't make it a lie intended to trick people into thinking that you love somebody.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T14:03:33-07:00","id":1151466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1151075-i-have-no-idea-how-to-use-solar-performance-and-bureaucracy?p=1151216#post1151216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It feels like most gods (and elemental?) has a positive Intimacy toward music and dance, there is an Artifact fans and erhu that can be used to attract spirits near you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Demons, ghosts and unclassifiables too, if going by RAW. What as an aside makes me think of some silly scenario involving a performer-exorcist that pulls out hidden critters out of woodwork with some peculiar brand of display (pleasing or grating to their nature, your choice) flutist of hamlin style.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1151075-i-have-no-idea-how-to-use-solar-performance-and-bureaucracy?p=1151216#post1151216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can definitely imagine a bunch of good scenes coming out of this idea. There is a sleeping Elemental Dragon near An-teng who will go on a rampage when he wakes up, I plan to just smack him around at first when I read about him, but I wonder if some heartfelt song would work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now going on a bit of trivia, there's an occult charm - Burning Exorcism Technique - that lets a solar treat diseases or derangements as spirits to be exorcised, captured or anything else the exalt might try to play at with a spirit, with its evolutions, Soul Projection Method and Immortal Soul Vigil, making it possible for one to enter other beings and combat such and other conditions in surreal inner mindscapes.<br /> <br /> Considering solar Performance charms are all about mind, emotions and special effects, i think making some charm cascade playing on this theme of &quot;drawing forth vistas from the soul unto the world&quot; or something along such lines might be appropriate and interesting, imho.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1151075-i-have-no-idea-how-to-use-solar-performance-and-bureaucracy?p=1151216#post1151216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both Orpheus and the girl in the Ex3 Performance's write-up uses this same trope i.e A musician uses their skill to make a person of authority feel emotional. It feels awesome since it happens only one time, but does it become stale if a Solar does this repeatedly?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, might not the same logic/problem sort of apply to Presence or Socialize, then?<br /> <br /> <br /> <i><b>Off-topic</b></i>: Jen, do you have some deviantart page, tumblr or somesuch to collect all those adorable short comics of yours? Because i would love to re-read a bunch of them at leisure and show to friends without having to track them down throughout dozens of threads in the forum. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 01-22-2019, 09:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T18:04:17-07:00","id":1151513,"title":"","content":"For Performance, see any musical number from a Disney movie.<br /> <br /> Be Our Guest, if you want to be specific","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T19:54:21-07:00","id":1151540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1151075-i-have-no-idea-how-to-use-solar-performance-and-bureaucracy?p=1151513#post1151513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Performance, see\u2026 Be Our Guest, if you want to be specific</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't call &quot;tantalizing a hungry person by waving food in front of their nose and singing for five minutes&quot; the high-water mark of Solar Performance.<br /> <br /> (Nor do I particularly see Lumiere as a Solar.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 10-20-2017, 11:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T18:34:28-07:00","id":1151807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1151075-i-have-no-idea-how-to-use-solar-performance-and-bureaucracy?p=1151540#post1151540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't call &quot;tantalizing a hungry person by waving food in front of their nose and singing for five minutes&quot; the high-water mark of Solar Performance.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I recall she somehow was fed by that song and one small bit of &quot;the gray stuff&quot;, I'd call that impressive :P<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (Nor do I particularly see Lumiere as a Solar.) </div> </div> </div>...<br /> *sigh* Fair enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T19:06:27-07:00","id":1151813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1151075-i-have-no-idea-how-to-use-solar-performance-and-bureaucracy?p=1151807#post1151807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I recall she somehow was fed by that song\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Was</i> she, though, or was she just too polite to say, &quot;Hey, this song-and-dance stuff is great and all, but I'm almost to the point of passing out here, please <b>feed me</b>?&quot;<br /> <br /> (We also don't typically see characters do a lot of things in musicals, but I don't think it's supposed to imply that singing songs will magically fill your belly or void your bowels.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 10-21-2017, 10:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T09:21:20-07:00","id":1151954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anathemouse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sol