a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T10:26:35-07:00","id":1151968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1151075-i-have-no-idea-how-to-use-solar-performance-and-bureaucracy?p=1151954#post1151954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do have a <a href=\"http://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Tumblr </a>page for easy viewing.</div> </div> </div> </div>The artwork of which is most easily found in <a href=\"http://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/myart\" target=\"_blank\">here </a>, btw.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T15:11:26-07:00","id":1152041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1151075-i-have-no-idea-how-to-use-solar-performance-and-bureaucracy?p=1151954#post1151954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh yeah, like Hermes causing Argus to slumber with his music. Does something like that make sense for Solar's Performance I wonder?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I do have a <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/&amp;quot;]Tumblr</a> [/URL]page for easy viewing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder, is making someone Sleepy with an Inspire, and then them acting on that would be them going to sleep? <br /> <br /> I too have been curious about a Jen collection. Love the art, and want to see what these characters get up to. Thanks","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T18:11:35-07:00","id":1152081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1151075-i-have-no-idea-how-to-use-solar-performance-and-bureaucracy#post1151075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, if Dai Sifu does decide to sing in a public place in city X</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI intended to bring up the point about Azhrarn being haunted by a song depicting a world without humanity up somehow, but when I looked closely enough at the post to see this line, I was suddenly struck by the image of the musical episodes from the first three episodes of Angel Beats.<br /> <br /> It's a very melancholic feeling.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still uncertain about how various characters/places in Creation think about music?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bOh now there you ask too broad of a question, far too broad.<br /> <br /> &quot;There are not more than five musical notes, yet the combinations of these five give rise to more melodies than can ever be heard.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T20:31:45-07:00","id":1152101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1151075-i-have-no-idea-how-to-use-solar-performance-and-bureaucracy?p=1152081#post1152081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bOh now there you ask too broad of a question, far too broad.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bSuddenly I am afraid that this response is both misunderstanding your question, and simply unhelpful.<br /> <br /> To be direct:<br /> <br /> \u200bJen, I am afraid that I do not understand what you mean when you say you're uncertain about what the setting thinks of music, or the meaning of the example with the bird-woman death god. I genuinely wish to understand.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T21:56:51-07:00","id":1152107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1151075-i-have-no-idea-how-to-use-solar-performance-and-bureaucracy?p=1152101#post1152101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Suddenly I am afraid that this response is both misunderstanding your question, and simply unhelpful.<br /> <br /> To be direct:<br /> <br /> Jen, I am afraid that I do not understand what you mean when you say you're uncertain about what the setting thinks of music, or the meaning of the example with the bird-woman death god. I genuinely wish to understand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so in ancient East Asian, there are only four jobs in society: The scholar, the farmer, the merchant and the craftmen. As you can see, artist and entertainer aren't on the list so they have to sit at the bottom of the social classes along with slave and criminal. There is a story in my country about \u0110\u00e0o Duy T\u1eeb who is forbidden from entering the imperial exam since his dad is an actor, the guy then later become a famous mandarin of the later dynasty, there is also the kisaeng in Korea who have to pay a hefty fine to buy their freedom. This despise the fact that playing an instrument is considered by Confucius to be a mark of a true man.<br /> <br /> I'm wondering if Creation has a diverse opinion on entertainer like Earth, since from reading the books it seems like everyone loves someone who has high Performance, even Varang with its oppressive social ladder only confuses about actor and musician. The death god example is me uncertain if something hostile to Performance like that can exist in Creation when spirits seems to like dancing, music and theatre so much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 10-23-2017, 07:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T04:29:22-07:00","id":1152156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1151075-i-have-no-idea-how-to-use-solar-performance-and-bureaucracy?p=1152107#post1152107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm wondering if Creation has a diverse opinion on entertainer like Earth, since from reading the books it seems like everyone loves someone who has high Performance, even Varang with its oppressive social ladder only confuses about actor and musician. The death god example is me uncertain if something hostile to Performance like that can exist in Creation when spirits seems to like dancing, music and theatre so much.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bIt's an interesting question. It also puts me in mind of ancient Rome, where people would have often liked theatre, but had a very low opinion of actual actors.<br /> <br /> \u200bYour example of Asian cultures also has me wondering about variations depending on who is playing the instrument and why; the difference between the monarch playing the bells in ceremony to generate a tone harmonious with the universe, and the person who plays an instrument full time, whom people will denigrate even while they listen in.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo I wonder if it's possible to reconcile what the books might say with the notion that some of those people might love the performance, but not the performer.<br /> <br /> \u200bStill, I don't think that your idea would be a major contradiction of anything fundamental to the setting, so even if the books never portray it, if it's something you know of and want to portray, you know best what to do with it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T04:39:59-07:00","id":1152158,"title":"","content":"That said in exalted performance also covers speeches and stuff so anyone good with a musical instrument can also orate like a mofo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T04:53:35-07:00","id":1152159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1151075-i-have-no-idea-how-to-use-solar-performance-and-bureaucracy?p=1151216#post1151216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both Orpheus and the girl in the Ex3 Performance's write-up uses this same trope i.e A musician uses their skill to make a person of authority feel emotional. It feels awesome since it happens only one time, but does it become stale if a Solar does this repeatedly?</div> </div> </div> </div>Performance is entirely about moving, touching, enchanting, inspiring and despairing. Variants of it sure are useful, but odds are you'll stick to those.<br /> An Exalted performance could easily throw the entire audience into a near blind rage, for example. Or start an impromptu orgy worthy of Perfume.<br /> <br /> Starting a revolt, or quelling it, is most easily done by performance. A single song of sorrow and hope and honor may stop two armies in clash.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 10-23-2017, 07:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T05:00:28-07:00","id":1152161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1151075-i-have-no-idea-how-to-use-solar-performance-and-bureaucracy?p=1152158#post1152158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said in exalted performance also covers speeches and stuff so anyone good with a musical instrument can also orate like a mofo.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI prefer to think of it as being that any character has the <i>option</i> be such, but in many cases the Orichalcum rule applies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T05:43:51-07:00","id":1152168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1151075-i-have-no-idea-how-to-use-solar-performance-and-bureaucracy?p=1152158#post1152158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said in exalted performance also covers speeches and stuff so anyone good with a musical instrument can also orate like a mofo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but like Melee I think that people tends to stick with one aspect of the Abilities. I certainly didn't plan any oration-scene for my entertainer Zenith.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T05:50:04-07:00","id":1152170,"title":"","content":"Honestly this was one of the useful things about being able to buy a speciality three times in 2e. You could have a character that was really good at <i>one </i>aspect of an ability but only mediocre at anything else. <br /> <br /> Why did they change that, anyway?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T06:13:05-07:00","id":1152174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1151075-i-have-no-idea-how-to-use-solar-performance-and-bureaucracy?p=1152170#post1152170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly this was one of the useful things about being able to buy a speciality three times in 2e. You could have a character that was really good at <i>one </i>aspect of an ability but only mediocre at anything else. <br /> <br /> Why did they change that, anyway?</div> </div> </div> </div>Its notable effects are to reduce number bloat and resource sink, and making specialists not quite so out of the reach of generalists, so I bet those were the reasons.<br /> <br /> It doesn't prevent you from playing a character as focused in one aspect of the Ability, but that style is no longer as strongly incentivised. It makes the Exalted more broadly capable in many ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T13:45:11-07:00","id":1152286,"title":"","content":"It also leads to a certain kind of stat bloat where rather than having characters who have like, Archery 2 (+3 Firewands) you actually just get everyone with Archery 5 (+3 Firewands) leading to dice pools even more bloated than they might otherwise be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T14:51:47-07:00","id":1152301,"title":"","content":"In my version of Creation, performers of whichever sort can operate at many levels of social standing, depend on prowess and reputation. If they're good enough, and they do a good enough job of building contacts and connections, and luck out a little, they can even sometimes gain minor titles (in some places). It's not common, but it's not unknown either. It's also considered a mark of refinement to be able to entertain one's friends. This is a setting without recorded entertainment, remember.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T15:05:28-07:00","id":1152308,"title":"","content":"I do imagine that one thing that would be common to the Blessed Isle and many societies throughout the Threshold is that your successful performer might be living more off of patronage than independently wealthy. It's a common model for how many earlier social and economic models process such people, and have them indelibly tied to conspicuous consumption.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt would be part of why multiple societies have equated performers with prostitution, even apart from how such systems are rife with the potential for sexual abuse.<br /> <br /> \u200bI mean, not that the 20th-21st century entertainment industry was much different in that regard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T22:06:58-07:00","id":1152409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1151075-i-have-no-idea-how-to-use-solar-performance-and-bureaucracy?p=1152168#post1152168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, but like Melee I think that people tends to stick with one aspect of the Abilities. I certainly didn't plan any oration-scene for my entertainer Zenith.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might still be worth looking at the charms for other abilities, either as inspiration for the types of things one can do with Performance or because Penultimate Unity of Form is a thing. Especially if you can talk your ST into unifying all the repetitive double 9s charms into one, picking up PUF opens up a lot of flexibility.<br /> <br /> Dance a staccato rhythm in time with a storm, but apply Seventeen Cycles Symphony so that, as you transition to a stately waltz, so too does the storm settle into a gentle rain, give an encouraging speech with Battle Anthem to rouse the fighting spirit of your allies, or even fuse Shining Expression Style with Seven Thunders Voice through music to inspire an entire city to think of those they love most with just a soothing serenade.<br /> <br /> I've had a lot of fun as a player sticking just to Oratory stuff, but I recently noticed PUF for the first time, and I have to say: having a way to do other discipline's signature sorts of things backed by charms has opened up a lot of space in the way I think about using the ability","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12145-arion-wind","name":"Arion Wind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T22:10:40-07:00","id":1152410,"title":"","content":"My favorite Performance Charm for this edition has got to be Phantom-Conjuring Performance. You remember in your comics, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar298_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"298\" data-vbnamecard=\"298\">Jen</a>, where you do flashbacks to the Sun giving over the Mandate of Heaven to the Solar Exalted? With this Charm, you can have the characters listening to the story actually <i>see</i> those flashbacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T05:36:38-07:00","id":1152473,"title":"","content":"Well, to discuss the Bureaucracy side of the question here...<br /> <br /> One of my characters was a 'typical' filthy-rich (Resources 5) Bureacracy-Supernal Eclipse, and he was more or less the linchpin of the group. Owned his own island in the West, and a lot of plots revolved around his island and his fleet. (He had both Merchant and non-Merchant Bureaucracy Charms.)<br /> <br /> Anyway, from a plot perspective, Bureaucracy is not generally an in-your-face Ability, and shares an 'indirect approach' with Socialize and other Abilities. Bureaucracy is not the brute force of Presence or even Performance, but it is all about setting things up socially--particularly on a large scale--so that the menu of options available to you is more favorable than the menu of options available to your opponent. Someone trying to bribe someone else? Offer a larger bribe. Can't? Wreak havoc with the briber's bank accounts so that he cannot make good on the bribe. <br /> <br /> One recent (non-Solar) example is the political infighting among the Dynasty between Sesus and Tepet to make the war against the Bull as excruciating as possible. In <i>general</i>, the larger your undertaking in Creation, the more important Bureacracy (and its Charms) can be. If you plan on taking on the Dynasty, fomenting ongoing paralysis in their bureaucracy will slow any possible response to your actions. <br /> <br /> A good 'character concept' for a traveling Bureaucrat besides troubleshooter--which is still tied to a single organization, generally--is an Ambassador. You'd probably want Socialize and Linguistics as well, but Bureaucracy is crucial for <i>managing</i> things. Oh, I'm in treaty negotiations and there's a third party also angling for the same treaty? Sorry if your messages all go awry (Indolent Official Charm) while mine have no problem (Speed the Wheels). The speed advantage involved with such things cannot be understated, and if you want to RP the negotiations rather than the messages going back and forth, it's unlikely that there will be Essence users you're using as couriers.<br /> <br /> I think a good TV example of a Solar Eclipse that uses Bureaucracy well is Col. Hogan from Hogan's Heroes (I am currently rewatching the show). Sure, he's a fast-talking action con artist, but he can be seen as having both positive Bureaucracy (just check out the extensiveness of his underground system and how he processes prisoners 'like clockwork') and negative Bureaucracy (Stalag 13 never runs well) aspects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3551-ulthwithian","name":"Ulthwithian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T02:26:49-07:00","id":1155004,"title":"","content":"I wonder if you could make your enemies dance with resonance of the building, bringing it down on them. Something like <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Angers_Bridge\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Angers_Bridge</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/744-korusef","name":"Korusef","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar744_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"510"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T03:02:06-07:00","id":1155007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korusef</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1151075-i-have-no-idea-how-to-use-solar-performance-and-bureaucracy?p=1155004#post1155004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if you could make your enemies dance with resonance of the building, bringing it down on them. Something like <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Angers_Bridge\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Angers_Bridge</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really care if it's possible or not. It would just be too epic to not let it happen.<br /> <br /> (just remember to buy Seven Shadow Evasion)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>French Exalt &amp; ST &amp; ToolMaker [<a href=\"http://refhi.free.fr/\" target=\"_blank\">Website</a>]<br /> Advanced Character Generator <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1087290-advanced-character-generator#post1087290\" target=\"_blank\">Thread, </a><a href=\"http://refhi.free.fr/exalted3/Fiche%20perso%20colab.xlsx\" target=\"_blank\">Excel Version</a> &amp; <a href=\"http://refhi.free.fr/exalted3/Fiche%20perso%20colab.ods\" target=\"_blank\">LibreOffice Version</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141199-exalted-3-familiar-generator\" target=\"_blank\">Familiar Generator Thread</a> &amp; <a href=\"http://refhi.free.fr/exalted3/Familiar%20Generator.ods\" target=\"_blank\">Libreoffice Version</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13355-refhi","name":"Refhi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13355_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"147"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T05:45:05-07:00","id":1155025,"title":"","content":"\u2026does anyone else wanna see a follow-up to Jen's comic?<br /> <br /> 'Cuz I do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T08:31:29-07:00","id":1155074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1151075-i-have-no-idea-how-to-use-solar-performance-and-bureaucracy?p=1152170#post1152170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly this was one of the useful things about being able to buy a speciality three times in 2e. You could have a character that was really good at <i>one </i>aspect of an ability but only mediocre at anything else.<br /> <br /> Why did they change that, anyway?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the main reason was that optimized characters always went Attribute 5 + Ability 5 + Specialty 3. Because you could only have three Specialties, every character had only one or maybe two closely related specialties - swords and fighting with two weapons, for example. This base of 13 dice contributed to number bloat and so on.<br /> <br /> \u200bIf you want to bring back the old stacking specialties without breaking the game in half, you need just a few things. First, every Specialty beyond the first needs to be more expensive in a manner similar to how normal Ability dots work. I'd recommend trying to price it so that it's about half the cost of an Ability dot. Second, the maximum number of dice you can get from Ability + Specialties is 6. Put those two house rules in place and you should be able to have eight Specialties in one Ability without any problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}